# Files that exist to develop this extension, not to run it.
#
# `specify extension add --dev` copies this directory verbatim into a consuming
# project's `.specify/extensions/adrkit/`. Everything below is build- or
# test-time only, and shipping it means depositing our scaffolding in someone
# else's repository. A governance tool that litters the repo it is supposed to
# help govern does not stay installed.
#
# Gitignore semantics (upstream parses this with pathspec.GitIgnoreSpec).

# Test suite and its TypeScript project.
test/
tsconfig.json

# Workspace metadata. The installed extension is driven entirely by
# extension.yml; package.json exists for the Bun workspace, not for consumers.
package.json

# Never ship a dependency tree. Bun's isolated linker would put workspace
# symlinks here, which aborts the install partway through rather than merely
# cluttering it. The package declares no dependencies precisely so this stays
# empty, but excluding it is the belt to that suspenders.
node_modules/
